# The Quiet Archive - EP08 An Evening in Ancient Athens (c. 430s BC, the age of Pericles)
# New scenes: "acropolis" = the rock of the Acropolis seen from the lower town at dusk: the Parthenon's columns and
# pediment pale in the moonlight, the bronze Athena with a glint on her spear tip, terracotta-roofed houses with lit
# courtyards climbing the slope, olive trees, and a little owl that glides across the sky once per loop (_owl);
# "pnyx" = from the rocky Pnyx hill: the city spread below with lamplit doorways, the Acropolis to one side, the Long
# Walls running down to the Piraeus with harbour lights and the sea; Hymettus glowing violet; an owl perched on a rock;
# "stoa" = the Agora at lamplighting: a long two-storey colonnade with hanging lamps, plane trees, a herm, the round
# Tholos with one lit door, stall awnings being folded; "courtyard" = an Athenian house courtyard: whitewashed mudbrick
# walls, a doorway herm, a small altar with a curl of incense, a well-head, a fig tree, a loom in the portico, amphorae;
# "andron" = the men's dining room at a quiet symposium: couches along the walls, figures reclining, a mixing bowl on a
# stand, lamps on tall stands, a painted frieze band and a doorway onto the moonlit court.
# New "moths" particles (soft pale moths drifting round the lamps); palette key "terra" (terracotta) and "marble".
